[103.740928, "i", "Role('b', '', ('a',))})\n        self.assertEqual(catalog.expand(['a', 'b']), ['a', 'b'])\nPY\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('README.md')\ns = p.read_text()\na = s.index('## Known gaps (0.4)')\nb = s.index('## Handoffs', a)\ns = s[:a] + '''## Handler status\n\nThe former 0.4 gaps are implemented and covered by regression tests:\nrevocations, transitive/idempotent grants, comma-separated roles, normalized\nsender addresses, held/rejected audit entries, and write-free dry runs. Dry runs\nsimulate the whole queue in memory, including minimum-holder checks.\n\nDelegation uses only the single `From` mailbox, never Cc, display names, quoted\napprovals, or signature text. Multiple/malformed From addresses are rejected.\n`trusted_authserv_ids` in `policy/delegation.toml` optionally identifies trusted\nmail gateways: an explicit DMARC failure reported by one holds the request for\nmanual verification, even when From names a delegated sender. The ingress must\nstrip forged Authentication-Results headers claiming its o"]
[103.740945, "i", "wn ID. Missing\nresults remain compatible with local form messages; this is not a replacement\nfor authentication at the mail gateway.\n\n''' + s[b:]\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n"]
